==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Lilin, type π''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Lilin π''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
A decent attacker against Angel and Aku enemies with average survivability, but not enough range to be particularly safe to use. Against [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]], Lilin's abilities do not stand out compared to other units, but she can still be used quite effectively against both enemy backliners such as [[Sunfish Jones]] and common Angels like [[Angelic Gory]]. Against Aku, she is far more interesting thanks to her ability to pierce their Shields on every attack, making her the go-to Uber for [[Aku Cyclone]] as she dramatically reduces its effective HP. The more dangerous Aku enemies tend to be backliners with a lot of damage, pushing power and range, which balances the ability by making her fairly risky to use despite the strength. On top of that, without [[Surge Attack|Surge]] [[Immune to Surge|immunity]], she will have to deal with the [[Death Surge]]s of the Aku she kills.

==='''True Form'''===
Her True form improves her health and gives her the ability to create a level 1 Surge Attack. Her problems are only slightly fixed, as the Surge has an extremely wide spawn area, meaning it may not appear when it counts, although when it does, certain enemies like [[Ackey]] and [[Wicked Face]] do become easier to handle. Her increased health can help her tank a few more hits from Surges or [[Fallen Bear]] and gives her a better chance to break a Shield before dying, but despite the health increase, her usage doesn't change against Angels as her damage remains subpar. Luckily, the increase in the amount of difficult Aku stages have escalated ever since and will likely see further increases in the future, meaning despite the extreme True Form cost and the few utility scenarios, her True Form may still be worth getting.

The other notable gain in her True Form is a single-slot [[Cat Cannon]] Recharge [[Cat Combo|Combo]], which is efficient for what it does, and when combined with other, similar Combos, can allow more frequent Cat Cannon attacks. This will make all the difference when necessary, such as against [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]-heavy stages where you'll be using Holy Blast frequently.

==='''Talents'''===
Lilin's Talents are all fairly mediocre across the board for their cost, and hardly improve her overall performance.

Her most notable Talent is [[Immune to Weaken]], which prevents groups of [[Mr. Angel]]s and [[Miz Devil]]s from halving her attack; she can also reliably counter [[Winged Pigge]] and [[Archangel Exiel]] whenever relevant. Otherwise, it rarely impacts significant matchups and serves primarily as a failsafe for hyperspecific enemies.

[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Slow]] is rather interesting, since Angel and Aku have a small variety of enemies that can [[Slow]] your units. Notably, she is less likely to be stunlocked by [[Condemned Peng]]'s [[Death Surge]]s, [[Tarsiriel]] and [[Sunfish Jones]]. However, these situations are so niche that it is ill-advised to unlock this Talent solely for that reason.

Finally, [[Freeze]] could have had the potential to turn Lilin into a decent crowd-controller for her target traits, but its mediocre activation rate and uptime give it only a 1/6 uptime at all times, severely diminishing its effectiveness. At 235 NP, this Talent is hardly worth the investment.

Since Lilin is a stat-based unit that relies on tanking damage and dishing out punishment, Attack Buff and HP Buff are by far her most worthwhile Talents.

